  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, far outperforming config_010 (image-only, ResNet50) at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether the learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) improves over the linear PCA baseline, which is a fundamental representation choice. This experiment (config_004) isolates exactly that variable: same model setting (RNA-only), same profile setting (single-profile), same architecture, but swapping PCA n2000 for scvi_n200. If scvi_n200 matches or beats PCA, it signals that learned nonlinear representations add value and justifies further investment in advanced encoders (scgpt) and multimodal fusion with better RNA features. If PCA remains superior, it tells us the signal is largely linear and we should focus budget on profile/aggregation or fusion strategies rather than encoder complexity. This is the cleanest single-variable comparison available and the highest-information experiment before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

